# LeakSanitizer suppressions.
#
# match_criterion / parse_one_criterion cache a compiled regex_t in a
# thread-local across calls so OP_REGEX scans don't pay regcomp() per
# record. The pthreads pool workers live until process shutdown and
# we don't currently install a thread-exit destructor to regfree() the
# cache — so on process exit ASan sees the regex_t's internal mallocs
# as leaked. Bounded total: one regex_t per pool worker × ~512 bytes
# ≈ 8 KB on a default 16-worker pool; OS reclaims at exit. To remove
# this suppression, install a pthread_key_create destructor that
# regfree's the cache on thread exit (~20 LOC) — tracked as future work.
leak:match_criterion
leak:parse_one_criterion
